{:records [] :evidence [{:evidence/at "2026-09-24T16:20:01.051116340Z" :evidence/author "joe" :evidence/body {:clocked-mission "M-autoclock-in" :clocked-target "M-autoclock-in" :event "chat-turn" :mission-id "M-autoclock-in" :role "user" :text "So, we don't need to redirect claude-1 or claude-10 \"live\" but we should create an enforcement rule similar to the inbox-zero followup: message that says \"You can't use Kimi without sending a work target\" or similar.  Indeed, the usual use case I have in mind is that the calling agent (say, claude-1) should clock in on something and then just send that as its work target for Kimi.  This is why I'm saying that if M-autoclock-in features actually worked, we wouldn't have to think about this much.  If claude-10 stays stuck on M-futon-seams even if work drifts to another topic, the risk is that it keeps calling Kimi with M-futon-seams as the work target and never triggers a compaction." :transport "emacs-claude-repl" :turn-id "claude-11-turn-3"} :evidence/claim-type "question" :evidence/id "emacs-46e69c9bcb4fad45e86fd6a63e649a84" :evidence/in-reply-to "emacs-4a1aabd760c10d7aa31b139e9ccc091b" :evidence/session-id "85fc3016-f51c-4083-bcc6-5a0f8e22cb11" :evidence/subject {:ref/id "85fc3016-f51c-4083-bcc6-5a0f8e22cb11" :ref/type "session"} :evidence/tags ["claude" "chat" "turn" "user"] :evidence/type "coordination"} {:evidence/at "2026-09-24T16:28:10.181607946Z" :evidence/author "joe" :evidence/body {:clocked-mission "M-autoclock-in" :clocked-target "M-autoclock-in" :event "chat-turn" :mission-id "M-autoclock-in" :role "user" :text "Let's look into these issues a bit more carefully.  128k should be considered a placeholder.  And the real issue is the target gate.  TBH it could be as simple as requiring a one-line requisition request that includes the mission name in each call, agents shouldn't have a hard time with that." :transport "emacs-claude-repl" :turn-id "claude-11-turn-6"} :evidence/claim-type "question" :evidence/id "emacs-b8292f5d0dd1a1d808cc859285150956" :evidence/in-reply-to "emacs-287c353c3613aea38802c1cc821563a5" :evidence/session-id "85fc3016-f51c-4083-bcc6-5a0f8e22cb11" :evidence/subject {:ref/id "85fc3016-f51c-4083-bcc6-5a0f8e22cb11" :ref/type "session"} :evidence/tags ["claude" "chat" "turn" "user"] :evidence/type "coordination"}]}
